name: IaC child source and literal paths remain distinct through Review, export and restart
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/iac_child_source.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME prepare
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
paste-file: @ART/open-literal.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 "client\\scope/Dockerfile":1 | literal-child-finding
expect: Dockerfile pins a base image
expect-not: Map ✓
expect-not: Enter run plan
ask: Does the actual IaC signal retain the literal child path and source identity without claiming Map completion or a verified vulnerability?
submit: logs
paste-file: @ART/run-nested.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 35 iac-scan: 1 finding | nested-child-scan
paste-file: @ART/run-literal.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 35 iac-scan: 1 finding | repeated-literal-scan
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/iac_child_source.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME direct
type: preserve IaC audit draft
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/iac_child_source.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME sast-run
require-live-snap: 25 preserve IaC audit draft | external-scans-keep-draft
ask: Do two explicit headless SAST scans preserve the composer and the same two child findings, with no model request, duplicate finding or source substitution?
keys: C-u
paste-file: @ART/run-whole.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 35 iac-scan: 2 findings | whole-source-scan
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/iac_child_source.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME whole
paste-file: @ART/open-literal.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 "client\\scope/Dockerfile":1 | literal-source-review
submit: decision deferred Owned mutable-image policy awaits owner review
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: deferred | literal-decision
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/iac_child_source.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME reviewed
resize: 160x48
live-snap: literal-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: literal-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: literal-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: literal-60x20
nav-mode:
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 q review list | literal-source-reader
resize: 40x12
live-snap: literal-40x12
expect: "client\\scope/Dockerfile":1
keys: NPage
live-snap: literal-page-1
keys: NPage
live-snap: literal-page-2
keys: NPage
live-snap: literal-page-3
keys: NPage
live-snap: literal-page-4
ask: Across six sizes and source paging, can the operator distinguish the literal directory from the nested neighbor and read the retained source and deferral?
resize: 120x36
keys: q
paste-file: @ART/open-nested.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 client/scope/Dockerfile:1 | nested-source-review
expect-not: recorded: deferred
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 scope paths . | report
expect: 3 inspected files
expect-not: scope not recorded
keys: j j j
require-live-snap: 20 format json | json-report
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 EXPORTED | exported
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/iac_child_source.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME exported
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
paste-file: @ART/open-literal.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 "client\\scope/Dockerfile":1 | recovered-literal
expect: recorded: deferred
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/iac_child_source.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME restarted
ask: Does no-color restart preserve the literal finding's source and decision, six real local scans, seven observations and two distinct findings without another scan or accepted phase?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
